{
  "id": 168,
  "Specification": "Solution to the readers-writers problem using a FIFO waiting queue to fairly serve read and write requests. Actors enqueue read or write requests; ReadOrWrite dequeues the head of the queue and either grants a read (set union) or write (only when no readers are present); StopActivity removes an actor. Properties: Safety (no readers and writers concurrently, at most one writer) and Liveness (every actor infinitely often enters and leaves both readers and writers).",
